WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.848
"The Side Effects of Artificial Food Coloring
and Dyes: Cancer and ADHD"

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.280
Nearly 50 years ago,

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.760
Cedars-Sinai Chief of Pediatrics
Ben Feingold,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.800
published heresy,

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.800
suggesting that
artificial food colors

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.960
could induce
behavioral disturbances.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.800
Dow Chemical disagreed,
as did Coca Cola,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.840
as well as other players

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.840
within the trillion-dollar
processed food industry,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.440
who were able to convince
the medical establishment

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.160
that it was all just one
elaborate placebo effect.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.320
But the truth can only be buried
so long.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.320
In 2004,
a randomized, double-blind,

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.040
placebo-controlled
food challenge was published.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.160
Hyperactivity in preschoolers
was significantly reduced

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.400
when artificial colorings

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.640
and the preservative
sodium benzoate

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.960
were eliminated
from their diets;

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.960
but hyperactivity
jumped back up

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.920
when the additives,
rather than a placebo,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.200
were reintroduced
into their diets.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
The researchers suggest
the benefit would accrue

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.720
for all children
if they didn't consume

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:07.840
artificial food colors
or benzoate preservatives.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.520
Then another randomized,
double-blind,

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.440
placebo-controlled
food challenge was published

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.960
in probably the most prestigious
medical journal in the world.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.040
This time, researchers found
that artificial colors

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.760
and other food additives
in processed foods

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:22.320
appeared to exacerbate
hyperactive behaviors;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.680
impulsivity, inattentiveness,
and overactivity,

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.200
among young children,

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.440
with more pronounced effects
in 3-year-olds

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.280
relative to 8-or 9-year-olds.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.640
And indeed, a more recent
randomized controlled trial

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.800
in 8- or 9-year-olds
in Hong Kong

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.240
didn't observe
a significant effect.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.760
The authors suggested
it may be

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.400
because older kids
may be less sensitive,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.800
or the dose used
was too small

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.840
relative to what
the kids typically consumed.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:51.080
But what happens in children
already diagnosed with ADHD

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.560
if you remove
artificial food colors?

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.920
In a meta-analysis
of randomized controlled trials

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.560
for dietary interventions
for ADHD,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.440
excluding artificial food colors
from the diet

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.560
significantly improved behavior.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.080
In this meta-analysis,

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:10.520
the data over here suggest
that food colors were harmful,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.160
whether assessed by parents,
observers,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.520
or attention tests,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.480
compared to studies
showing the opposite.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.600
You can actually see
the difference in brain waves

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.480
on EEG compared to placebo.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.200
As I highlighted years ago,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.120
the European Union
requires warning labels

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.800
of potential adverse effects
on activity and attention

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.160
in children.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.120
However, although
the Food and Drug Administration

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.120
in the United States has banned
a few artificial colors

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.760
like Red Dye No.1,
Red Dye No. 2,

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.240
Red Dye No. 4
due to cancer concerns,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.760
no warning labels are required,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.160
and many artificial colors

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:47.040
still predominate
processed foods.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.840
Among grocery store products
marketed to children,

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.800
about 40 percent contain
at least one artificial color.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.760
In 2021,

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:59.840
a report from the California
Environmental Protection Agency

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.640
highlighted the potential
neurobehavioral effects

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.960
of artificial food dyes
in children.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:05.880
The authors concluded

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.720
that although not all studies
implicated them,

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.160
the current medical literature

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.560
provides a substantial amount
of evidence

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.960
that consumption
of synthetic food dyes

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.520
is associated with adverse
neurobehavioral outcomes

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.640
in kids,

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.320
and the FDA's
Acceptable Daily Intake levels

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.440
may not adequately
protect children.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.640
For years I've been concerned
that Red No. 3

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.640
still hasn't been banned
from food,

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.000
given that it was banned
more than 30 years ago

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.760
from inclusion in any products
that go on our skin

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.320
due to cancer risk.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.480
Finally, in October 2023,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.960
the California Food Safety Act
was signed,

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.480
banning Red Dye No. 3
from foods and drinks

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:46.240
sold throughout the state,

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.480
while consumer groups,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.880
including the Center for Science
in the Public Interest,

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:52.920
continue to petition the FDA
for a national ban

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.000
to prohibit use
of this carcinogen.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.800
And on January 15 2025,

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.360
35 years after it was
banned in cosmetics,

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:08.040
the FDA finally banned it
nationwide in food as of 2027

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:13.392
and in drugs as of 2028.

